[Desktop Entry]
# Todoist, as a Brave app-mode window.
#
# WHY NOT A REAL DESKTOP APP
# Todoist ship official Snap and AppImage builds, but both live outside pacman
# and need hand-updating -- the same shape of neglect that let the old `todoist`
# AUR CLI rot from 2023 until the API was switched off under it in Feb 2026.
# The community `todoist-wrapper` is unusable as packaged: it injects a CSP that
# blocks Todoist's own CDN (todoist.b-cdn.net), so nothing loads. Upstream #157,
# open since 2026-03-31.
#
# Brave is already here, already native Wayland, and already updates with the
# system. App mode gives a chromeless window with no tabs or address bar.
#
# ⚠️ --class is IGNORED in Chromium app mode; the WM class is generated from the
# URL and profile. StartupWMClass below is the real one, measured 2026-09-13.
# The Hyprland rule that routes this to workspace 3 matches the same string.
#
# Separate --user-data-dir on purpose: its own cookie jar and session, so this
# is a Todoist app rather than a browser window that happens to be logged in.
Type=Application
Name=Todoist
GenericName=Task Manager
Comment=Todoist in a dedicated Brave app window
Exec=brave --app=https://app.todoist.com --user-data-dir=/home/decoy/.local/share/brave-todoist
Icon=todoist
Terminal=false
Categories=Office;ProjectManagement;
Keywords=todo;tasks;todoist;gtd;
StartupWMClass=brave-app.todoist.com__-Default
StartupNotify=true
